{
  "borough": "Camden",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed mix of residential unit sizes, comprising a large preponderance of small 1-bedroom units, would not provide an appropriate range of sizes to meet housing need in the area, contrary to Policies SD1 (Quality of life) and H8 (Mix of units) of the London Borough of Camden Unitary Development Plan 2006.\r\n",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed 1-bedroom units without a direct external light or ventilation source to the bedrooms would introduce an unacceptable standard of internal amenity and fail to meet Council standards contrary to Policy H1 (New housing) of the London Borough of Camden Unitary Development Plan 2006.\r\n",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed new building would, by virtue of the inappropriate design of the front elevation and the excessive bulk, scale and massing of the rear elevation,  fail to either preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the Charlotte Street Conservation Area Contrary to Policies B1 (General design principles), B2 (Design and layout of developments large enough to change their context) and B7 (Conservation areas) of the London Borough of Camden Unitary Development Plan 2006.\r\n"
  ],
